WEBVTT

00:00:09,620 --> 00:00:15,300
I have a friend who would like to know what is feeding his cancer, but he is not interested in

00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:21,940
ulcerative medicine. Is there a test he could do to ask his oncologist? No, there isn't.

00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:28,340
There's some things that a person could do. And I think I write about it in my book about,

00:00:29,060 --> 00:00:37,300
I mean, you know, just do trial and error things. I mean, if you're on a, let's say a ketogenic type

00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:47,860
diet or, you know, a ketogenic like diet, and, you know, your successful tests are showing,

00:00:49,540 --> 00:00:54,820
you know, a curve upwards to be your cancer is getting worse. Well, then switch your diet,

00:00:54,820 --> 00:01:01,460
you know, do an opposite diet, do a juicing diet or something like that. So, you have to cut

00:01:01,460 --> 00:01:09,460
an experiment with that then and see, you know, what makes you feel best and what makes the,

00:01:09,460 --> 00:01:16,740
you know, the tumor change. Now, some people that have a tumor that is visual or visual or palpable,

00:01:16,740 --> 00:01:22,580
it's easier to know, hey, you know, when I eat this, it seems like when I've been comments from,

00:01:22,580 --> 00:01:28,500
from many of you, you know, with a breast tumor, when I eat such and such, you know, it feels like my

00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:34,820
tumor actually gets bigger and it feels irritated. So, I stay away from that. When I stick to this diet,

00:01:34,820 --> 00:01:40,100
it, I just feel better and it seems like my tumor is going in the right direction. That's,

00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:46,100
that's a fair way to do that. Now, if you have a cancer in your test cell tract and you have no way

00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:50,820
of palpating or knowing whether it's getting better or worse, then it makes it more difficult

00:01:50,820 --> 00:01:55,460
until you're dependent upon tests, but you can certainly, you know, run the tumor marker test

00:01:55,460 --> 00:02:03,060
for something like that to monitor progress.

